WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:06.618
Ride for three hours, and Telo Ride stays as light as it started.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.502
Each second writes one speed into a buffer sized for four hours, set aside when the

00:00:15.502 --> 00:00:16.551
ride begins.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.255
Totals are running sums, and boards hold only the riders on them now. Nothing grows

00:00:28.255 --> 00:00:29.403
with the ride.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.122
At the finish, the ride goes out with ten thousand eight hundred samples, one a

00:00:40.122 --> 00:00:40.775
second.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:52.640
A minute from the end of three hours, from a phone to the full screen.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:04.465
What the tests prove: one sample a second, and a buffer that holds the longest ride.

00:01:09.685 --> 00:01:14.288
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:19.145
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.816
every hill and interval.

00:01:21.161 --> 00:01:26.339
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:26.339 --> 00:01:31.787
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:31.787 --> 00:01:34.777
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:35.123 --> 00:01:37.615
A custom workout lives under Profile.
